course: dictionary
lesson: 1414
title: Careless: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around the word to find the clues. In «a careless mistake», the clue is mistake, so careless means not paying enough attention, often from rushing.
explain: Careless can also mean not caring about something. The Mole says «some VERY careless and forgetful person has left his door-scraper lying about» in the Wild Wood. Left lying about shows that someone did not think about where things went, so careless means not paying attention. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Careless can mean relaxed and natural, without effort, as in «careless happiness». Here nobody is trying hard to feel happy. The happiness comes easily. When you meet careless, check which of the three meanings fits the clues around it.
fact: Careless means not paying enough attention, so you make mistakes or cause harm.
fact: «Careless mistake» means a slip made by rushing, such as copying a number wrong in maths.
fact: «Careless of danger» means not caring or worrying about danger.
fact: «Careless happiness» means relaxed, natural happiness that takes no effort.
fact: Careless ends in -less, a consonant ending, and the root word care stays the same.
exercise: In maths, Sam writes «a careless mistake» on his test. What is a careless mistake? | A very large sum of money | *A mistake made from rushing, such as copying a number wrong | A question with no answer | A mistake made on purpose to get attention
exercise: «A careless hit can destroy a find that waited millions of years.» What might a careless hit do? | *Destroy a find | Clean the bones | Make the palaeontologist laugh | Keep the find safe
exercise: The Mole thinks someone has left a door-scraper lying in the Wild Wood. What does careless mean there? | Happy and full of joy | *Not paying attention, so things get left about | Relaxed and easy | Very quick and neat
test: «Careless happiness» means happiness that is what? | Shouted loudly | Hard to reach, after much work | Sad and gloomy | *Easy and natural, without effort
test: The word careless ends in which ending? | -ness | *-less | -ment | -ful
exam: Which sentence uses careless to mean not paying enough attention? | The careless dog was loud and wagged its tail | The sun felt careless and warm on the beach | *He left his bag on the bus, a careless mistake that cost him his lunch | She sang with careless happiness at the party
